WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.440
This is The Spread, your energy
markets briefing for Thursday,

2
00:00:03.520 --> 00:00:05.440
the twenty-sixth of November.

3
00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:08.640
This episode is written and read with AI.

4
00:00:08.680 --> 00:00:12.960
Houthi drones over Saudi Arabia's
Ras Tanura refinery reversed an early

5
00:00:13.040 --> 00:00:17.560
slide in crude on Wednesday and lifted
Brent above ninety-three dollars.

6
00:00:17.600 --> 00:00:22.040
Separately, a record share of large
product tankers is now hauling crude,

7
00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:25.493
which keeps the cost of moving
diesel and jet fuel high.

8
00:00:25.547 --> 00:00:29.760
On the markets. Brent was at ninety-three
dollars sixty a barrel by mid-morning

9
00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:33.280
in New York on Wednesday,
up two point four percent.

10
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.280
West Texas Intermediate was
at eighty-three dollars fifty,

11
00:00:36.320 --> 00:00:38.200
up one point eight percent.

12
00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:41.840
In the US, distillate stocks rose
to about one hundred and five point

13
00:00:41.920 --> 00:00:44.920
six million barrels in the week
to the twentieth of November,

14
00:00:44.960 --> 00:00:49.200
according to the EIA. European gas
storage was sixty-seven point eight

15
00:00:49.280 --> 00:00:53.400
percent full as of Tuesday, according
to Gas Infrastructure Europe.

16
00:00:53.440 --> 00:00:57.840
The Houthis say they struck Ras
Tanura, the kingdom's largest refinery.

17
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:00.040
Saudi Arabia's account is different.

18
00:01:00.080 --> 00:01:03.840
It says its air defences destroyed
four drones over the site on Wednesday

19
00:01:03.920 --> 00:01:07.920
morning, and coalition spokesman
Turki Al-Maliki said fragments fell

20
00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:11.800
from the interceptions, with no
injuries in an initial assessment.

21
00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:14.520
So the claim of a hit comes
from the Houthis alone,

22
00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:17.360
and Riyadh describes interceptions only.

23
00:01:17.480 --> 00:01:20.800
Nothing in the reports we've seen
today says whether any refinery units

24
00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:22.520
or loadings were affected.

25
00:01:22.560 --> 00:01:24.347
Crude turned on the news.

26
00:01:24.373 --> 00:01:27.480
Brent had been at ninety dollars
ten in early Asian trade,

27
00:01:27.520 --> 00:01:30.680
according to OilPrice dot
com, before the gains came,

28
00:01:30.720 --> 00:01:34.200
and Rigzone noted they came
in thin pre-holiday trading.

29
00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:37.760
If the Houthis can reach the Gulf
coast, both Saudi export coasts are

30
00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:42.400
exposed, since they've already ordered
ships out of Saudi Red Sea ports.

31
00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:46.200
Staying with shipping, the product
tanker market is being reshaped.

32
00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.533
A record seventy-five percent of the
global fleet of Long Range Two tankers,

33
00:01:50.587 --> 00:01:54.213
the big clean-product carriers,
is now hauling crude instead,

34
00:01:54.347 --> 00:01:56.120
according to OilPrice dot com.

35
00:01:56.160 --> 00:01:59.960
The number and share still in
clean trade are at record lows.

36
00:02:00.000 --> 00:02:01.640
It comes down to earnings.

37
00:02:01.680 --> 00:02:04.200
Crude pays better since
the Middle East disruption,

38
00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:07.040
so owners are moving these
ships into dirty trade,

39
00:02:07.120 --> 00:02:11.360
gCaptain reported. That leaves fewer
large clean tankers and keeps fuel

40
00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.973
freight expensive. Long-haul buyers
of diesel and jet carry that cost,

41
00:02:16.027 --> 00:02:18.840
and Europe most of all.
As of mid-November,

42
00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:22.960
Kpler said the transatlantic arbitrage
on medium range tankers was already

43
00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.013
shut for December arrivals.

44
00:02:25.067 --> 00:02:29.840
An update on Hormuz. Iran's Islamic
Revolutionary Guard Corps navy says

45
00:02:29.920 --> 00:02:34.000
two tankers hit mines early Wednesday
off the southern and eastern coasts

46
00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:36.480
of the strait, causing engine-room fires.

47
00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.080
It says both were on routes
Iran hasn't authorised.

48
00:02:40.560 --> 00:02:43.600
That's Iran's claim only,
and no ships have been named.

49
00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:47.840
On the other side of the water,
the Abu Dhabi National Oil Company,

50
00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:52.160
ADNOC, has restricted loaded crude
and product tankers entering waters

51
00:02:52.280 --> 00:02:56.160
near some major UAE export
hubs, Rigzone reported.

52
00:02:56.240 --> 00:02:59.280
Which hubs, and for
how long, wasn't given.

53
00:02:59.360 --> 00:03:03.600
For context on volumes, Kpler put
Hormuz flows at fifty-five percent

54
00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:07.440
of pre-war levels in a note
dated the nineteenth of November.

55
00:03:07.520 --> 00:03:11.920
It said Asian refiners are paying large
premiums for Atlantic Basin crude,

56
00:03:12.000 --> 00:03:16.160
and chasing term deals for next
year with QatarEnergy and ADNOC.

57
00:03:16.240 --> 00:03:20.480
Over in China, refiners are buying more
crude abroad to rebuild inventories

58
00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:24.400
after the price fall, according
to traders cited by Bloomberg.

59
00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:28.320
Sinopec alone has reportedly bought
about twenty million barrels of West

60
00:03:28.400 --> 00:03:31.360
African crude this month,
for December loading.

61
00:03:31.400 --> 00:03:35.760
For scale, all Chinese buyers together
take twenty to twenty-five million

62
00:03:35.840 --> 00:03:38.360
barrels from West Africa
in an average month.

63
00:03:38.720 --> 00:03:41.360
Purchases from the Middle
East and Brazil are up too.

64
00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:45.040
That extra demand lands
on Atlantic Basin grades,

65
00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:48.640
the same barrels other Asian buyers
are already paying premiums for.

66
00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:52.960
Turning to gas, British
households face a steep rise.

67
00:03:53.280 --> 00:03:57.280
Ofgem, the energy regulator, confirmed
the price cap will go from about

68
00:03:57.360 --> 00:04:00.880
one thousand seven hundred and twenty
pounds to about two thousand one

69
00:04:00.960 --> 00:04:04.960
hundred and seventy. The change
takes effect on the first of January,

70
00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:07.440
a rise of twenty-six percent.

71
00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:09.920
It's the highest level
in over three years,

72
00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:13.280
driven by wholesale gas
prices lifted by the war.

73
00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:15.280
Relief doesn't look close.

74
00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:19.120
Petronas expects the liquefied
natural gas market to stay relatively

75
00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.960
tight through next year.

76
00:04:21.000 --> 00:04:22.320
A few more things.

77
00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:26.400
Kazakhstan has joined Iraq in asking
OPEC plus to raise its assessed

78
00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:30.160
production capacity, Reuters reported,
citing people familiar with the

79
00:04:30.320 --> 00:04:33.120
matter. Kazakhstan hasn't commented.

80
00:04:33.200 --> 00:04:37.680
Rystad Energy's Jorge Leon called Sunday's
meeting one of the most complicated

81
00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:38.960
in years.

82
00:04:39.040 --> 00:04:43.600
Equinor signed an eighteen-year
gas supply deal with Germany's VNG.

83
00:04:43.640 --> 00:04:46.880
It's the longest Norwegian gas sale
since the Troll agreements of the

84
00:04:46.960 --> 00:04:48.480
mid-nineteen-eighties.

85
00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:52.320
Dynagas told the US Securities and
Exchange Commission that three hundred

86
00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:55.520
and ninety million dollars of
charter revenue is at risk.

87
00:04:55.600 --> 00:04:59.440
That's if it can't replace insurance
for two Yamal liquefied natural

88
00:04:59.520 --> 00:05:02.400
gas carriers before
British sanctions tighten.

89
00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:07.200
Back on US inventories, crude and
gasoline stocks also rose in that week,

90
00:05:07.280 --> 00:05:10.560
with commercial crude three percent
below its five-year average.

91
00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:14.720
Pump prices are easing, with gasoline
averaging about three dollars seventy

92
00:05:14.760 --> 00:05:18.400
a gallon as of Saturday, and
diesel still well above that.

93
00:05:18.720 --> 00:05:22.400
In Russia, Putin said the country
will respond to Ukraine's attacks on

94
00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:26.400
its refineries, and called the
domestic fuel market challenging.

95
00:05:26.600 --> 00:05:29.600
Reuters reports that a
consortium led by Todd Boehly,

96
00:05:29.680 --> 00:05:33.200
and backed by the US International
Development Finance Corporation,

97
00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:36.400
has signed a deal for
Lukoil's international assets.

98
00:05:36.440 --> 00:05:39.920
It would swap Lukoil securities
worth ten billion dollars,

99
00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:43.120
and neither side has made a
statement in the reports we've seen.

100
00:05:43.320 --> 00:05:47.360
Italy, meanwhile, told Kyiv it was
wrong to attack Russian ships in Libyan

101
00:05:47.440 --> 00:05:48.400
waters.

102
00:05:48.440 --> 00:05:52.800
Aramco and S-Oil inaugurated the
seven-billion-dollar Shaheen complex

103
00:05:52.880 --> 00:05:56.960
in Ulsan, South Korea. It has about
three point two million tonnes of

104
00:05:57.240 --> 00:05:59.640
capacity, with production
due from next year.

105
00:05:59.920 --> 00:06:03.440
Petrobras approved a five-year plan
worth one hundred and twenty-two

106
00:06:03.680 --> 00:06:06.560
billion dollars, starting
in twenty twenty-seven.

107
00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:10.400
About eighty-six billion of that
goes to exploration and production.

108
00:06:10.480 --> 00:06:14.000
The Baker Hughes US rig count
held at six hundred and seven.

109
00:06:14.080 --> 00:06:17.200
Oil rigs rose by one, to
four hundred and seventy.

110
00:06:17.280 --> 00:06:21.040
And Vår Energi raised about one
point one billion dollars in a share

111
00:06:21.400 --> 00:06:25.120
placement, after agreeing to buy
ConocoPhillips' Norway business.

112
00:06:25.200 --> 00:06:30.053
What to watch next. On Sunday, OPEC
plus meets on targets for next year,

113
00:06:30.107 --> 00:06:33.800
with Iraq and Kazakhstan disputing
their capacity assessments.

114
00:06:33.840 --> 00:06:37.520
Then on Tuesday the second of
December, the EIA's weekly figures for

115
00:06:37.600 --> 00:06:41.480
the week to the twenty-seventh will
show whether distillates build again.

116
00:06:41.520 --> 00:06:45.120
That's the brief. Sources for everything
you heard are in the show notes.
